Error [E0121]: `evens` was consumed by the binding `first`, so it can't be used here
  --> share_uncopyable_use_after_move.jet:9:11
    |
  9 |     print(evens.to_list())
    |           ^^^^^
  --> share_uncopyable_use_after_move.jet:7:14
    |
  7 |     first := evens
    |              ^^^^^ `evens` moved to the binding `first` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `evens` after the move, or give the binding `first` a copy with `evens.copy()` where it moved.
 Note: `evens` is one-pass — materialize it first with `evens.to_list()`, or create a fresh source for the second drive
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
